From bed7a8ac7f795ba16507a4b13ad322e13753daaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CADCraft contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 13:34:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tool Sets of your own: tabs read from support/toolsets/*.json

Each .json file in the toolsets folder of the support folder adds a Tool Sets
tab after Drafting and Modeling. A tool is a button that submits its `input` at
the command line as if typed (a command, a LISP command or a LISP expression),
after cancelling the running command. Its icon is a block of the current
drawing, drawn from the block definition (attribute definitions and objects on
layers that are off left out), so a symbol library needs no image files; a tool
can list several block names and the first one the drawing defines is drawn.

- crates/ui-egui/src/user_toolsets.rs: file format, capped parsing (16 files of
  256 KB, 32 groups of 128 tools, 40-character names), block icons cached per
  drawing revision, tab body with collapsible groups; no file system on wasm.
- Tool Sets tabs narrow to fit when user tabs are added.
- ui.toolsets.reload reads the files again and returns the tab names.
- The workspace remembers built-in tabs only; reading still refuses others.
- docs/customization.md: "Tool Sets of your own".
- Tests: parsing, caps, hostile input, file loading and name clashes, a tool
  submitting its lines and cancelling a running command.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
