+## Tool Sets of your own
+
+Each `.json` file in the `toolsets` folder of the support folder (on Windows
+`%APPDATA%\CADCraft\support\toolsets`, on macOS `~/Library/Application Support/CADCraft/support/toolsets`,
+on Linux `~/.config/cadcraft/support/toolsets`) adds a tab to the Tool Sets, after Drafting and
+Modeling. A tool is a button that submits its `input` at the command line, as if typed, after
+cancelling the command that is running: a command (`LINE`), a LISP command (`MYCMD`) or a LISP
+expression (`(my:tool "GATE")`); several lines are submitted one after another. `block` names a
+block, or lists several, whose definition in the current drawing is drawn as the button's icon
+(the first one the drawing defines); attribute definitions and objects on layers that are off are
+left out, as an inserted block shows them. A tool without a block the drawing defines shows its
+label.
+
+```json
+{
+  "name": "P&ID",
+  "groups": [
+    { "name": "Valves",
+      "tools": [
+        { "label": "Gate valve", "input": "(pid:tool \"VLV_GATE\")", "block": ["PIP_VLV_GATE", "ISA_VLV_GATE"] },
+        { "label": "Instrument", "input": "PIDINST", "block": "PIP_INST_FIELD" }
+      ] }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+The files are read when the Tool Sets first show; `ui.toolsets.reload` reads them again and
+returns the tab names. Files are read in name order; a tab named like a built-in one or like an
+earlier file is skipped, and problems are reported on the command line. Sizes are capped (16
+files of 256 KB, 32 groups of 128 tools, 40-character names). The workspace remembers the
+built-in tabs only: a user tab shown when CADCraft closes opens on Drafting next time. There is no
+support folder on the web, so no user tabs there.
+
